Moving this from #1920, as it's a separate issue. I propose that `space-before-function-parentheses` should not warn on generator function expressions at all, instead deferring to `generator-star`.

eslint incorrectly reports an error for this code:

``` js
class Album {
  constructor (name, artist, path) {
    this.name = name
    this.artist = artist
    this.path = path
    this.pictures = []
  }
}

module.exports = Album
```

Line 2: Missing space before function parentheses.

With this config:

``` json
{
  "space-before-function-parentheses": [2, "always"]
}
```

Related to #1920.
